  "id": "COMPOUND:30129 - PROTEIN:5858",
  "verbalization": "Alpha-Cedrene epoxide is implicated in the interaction with KB through a series of molecular targets, all of which are ultimately linked to KB. The evidence suggests that alpha-Cedrene epoxide acts as a target for MOVP-3, Cocosamide B, and Licochalcone D, which in turn have KB as their target. This indicates a chain of molecular interactions where alpha-Cedrene epoxide serves as a starting point, leading through different biochemical pathways to KB. The presence of multiple distinct targets (MOVP-3, Cocosamide B, and Licochalcone D) suggests that alpha-Cedrene epoxide may exert its effects through diverse mechanisms, potentially involving different cellular processes or pathways. The integration of these targets into a single pathway highlights the complexity of the relationship, emphasizing the role of alpha-Cedrene epoxide in modulating KB through a network of molecular interactions.",
